On Monday 26 May 2003 12:24, Peter wrote:
> Thanks!
>
> I had tried all possible combinations with left site Ctrl, Alt, Shift not
> realizing that the right Alt/Shift have different functions and I can see
> now that there are about 30 odd more characters to get out with those two
> keys, not found on US keyboard setting.
>
> What I have not found yet is "|". How do you pipe in German? No that I need
> it, just curious.
>
> Regards

The key just to the left of what is the 'Y' on the German keyboard ('Z' on the 
US keyboard) is the greater than-less than key. It also has the pipe symbol, 
so Alt-Gr-<. 

